WEBVTT

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:09.958
- You have a beautiful home, Mr Curry.
- I've lived here all my life.

00:00:10.208 --> 00:00:14.417
I inherited it from my mother.
A very distant woman.

00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:17.667
And being such a pillar
of the community, I can see why

00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:21.333
having that beast move in next door
would upset you so.

00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:25.625
I suppose I should be grateful
that it's only one bear.

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.792
Oh, but it always starts
with just one, Mr Curry.

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:32.333
Soon, the whole street
will be crawling with them.

00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.583
Drains clogged with fur.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.333
Buns thrown at old ladies.

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:39.750
Raucous all-night picnics.

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:43.750
- What can we do?
- I have certain connections.

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:47.500
If I can get hold of the bear, I can see
that he's sent where he belongs,

00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:49.625
- no questions asked.
- Really?

00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:55.083
But I can't do it alone. I need
a strong, capable man to help me.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.583
Me? Oh, now...

00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:00.333
If I start hanging around,
people will ask questions.

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:04.875
But you? You could keep an eye on him,
couldn't you? For me?

00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:08.042
Of course.

00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:12.417
Perfect. So you do that.
Soon as he's alone, we'll pounce.

00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:16.417
Fire her up, Mr Gruber.

00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:19.042
- You actually broke in?
- That's right.

00:01:19.125 --> 00:01:20.667
Sounds incredibly brave.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.750
There's a time for being boring and
annoying, and a time for being a man.

00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:27.792
Mr Brown dressed up as a lady
and someone stuck pins in him.

00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:29.125
- What?
- It's starting.

00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:30.792
- What was that?
- Doesn't matter.

00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:32.208
- In a dress?
- No!

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.458
Did look like a dress.

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:36.208
More of a housecoat.
Quite liberating, actually.

00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:39.542
Darkest Peru.
A vast, unexplored wilderness,

00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:42.542
shrouded in mystery. Until now!

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.708
Is that where you're from?

00:01:44.792 --> 00:01:47.750
Oh, Paddington, it's incredible.

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:30.875
Goodbye, Lucy.
Goodbye, Pastuzo.

00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:35.583
And if you ever make it to London,
you can be sure of a very warm welcome.

00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:37.917
I have learnt so much from these bears,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.958
but I wonder what, if anything,
they have learnt from me.

00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:46.833
Montgomery Clyde.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.500
Dear Aunt Lucy.
You'll never guess what.

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:55.750
Today I saw a film the explorer made
of Darkest Peru.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:03:01.083
I do miss our old home, although I'm
beginning to understand life in London.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:05.583
The Browns are a curious tribe,
but I rather like them.

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.208
The way Mr Brown
arranges his stationery.

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.625
The strange objects
Mrs Brown finds in her handbag.

00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:13.542
Ah! There you are.

00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.875
How Mrs Bird has a Hoover
for every occasion.

00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:21.542
That Judy can master any language.
Even bear.

00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:26.875
Wonderful pronunciation.

00:03:27.625 --> 00:03:30.875
And how Jonathan
can build almost anything

00:03:30.958 --> 00:03:33.250
using only Mr Brown's
educational old toys.

00:03:34.125 --> 00:03:35.833
This is amazing!

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:39.292
It's very strange.
I may be about to find the explorer,

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:42.333
but I'm actually beginning
to feel at home here.

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:45.292
Paddington, these books
contain the names and addresses

00:03:45.375 --> 00:03:47.125
of all the people who live in London.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.917
If we look up every "M Clyde",
we'll find your explorer.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.542
- Thank you, Mrs Brown.
- Let's get cracking.

00:03:52.625 --> 00:03:54.625
Wait for me.
I'll see if I can find anything

00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:56.417
about Captain Clyde in the library.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.417
I'll come with you. I need to refresh
our marmalade supplies.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.875
Shouldn't someone stay with Paddington?

00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:03.667
It's only for a few hours.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.125
You don't need to worry, Mr Brown.
I think I've got the hang of things.

00:04:08.083 --> 00:04:09.583
Well, you take care.

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:12.000
- Bye.
- Goodbye.

00:04:12.083 --> 00:04:14.208
Have you ever
driven one of those?

00:04:20.542 --> 00:04:21.792
Yes?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.125
- Yes?
- Honeypot, this is Fierce Eagle.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.167
- What?
- It's Mr Curry.

00:04:28.208 --> 00:04:30.875
I did suggest that we adopt code names.

00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:33.417
- Honeypot and Fierce Eagle.
- Yes, of course.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.083
Do you actually have anything to report,
Fierce...?

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.542
- Eagle.
- ..Eagle?

00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:38.667
Affirmative.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.042
The Furry Menace is home alone.
I repeat,

00:04:42.125 --> 00:04:44.750
the Furry Menace is home alone.

00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:46.250
I'm on my way.

00:04:48.708 --> 00:04:49.875
Honeypot.

00:04:50.542 --> 00:04:52.667
- I need to get on the roof.
- Yes.

00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:57.083
And after, I wondered if you'd like
to celebrate by dining with me.

00:04:57.125 --> 00:04:59.542
I have some meat-paste sandwiches
and pickles.

00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:01.792
- Sounds glorious.
- They went off on Tuesday

00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:05.083
-but you're normally alright for a week.
-Mr Curry. The roof?

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.250
M Clyde, M Clyde...

00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:14.167
Oh, dear. Erm...

00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:33.667
Erm...

00:06:13.625 --> 00:06:14.833
Erm...

00:06:18.417 --> 00:06:19.958
I'm coming!

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:25.000
Come on, bear.

00:06:25.792 --> 00:06:28.625
Just got a bit tied up
with the stationery.

00:06:28.917 --> 00:06:30.417
Come on, little bear.

